.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, partial reads included; also when the reader of stdout goes away
early.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error, such as a filter needing
.B \-\-attrs full
on a scan without it.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown flag, a bad value, a flag of a later release.
.TP
.B 3
The path does not exist.
.TP
.B 4
Permission denied on the root, or unreadable directories under
.BR \-\-strict .
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Ctrl\-C).
